WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.500
Light on one set of vagal sensory axons suppresses breathing in an anaesthetized

2
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:14.580
mouse. Light on another set makes the animal breathe fast and shallow.

3
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:18.100
We follow only the sensory axons here.

4
00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:24.020
If the vagus were one cable reporting that the body is stretched, both results could

5
00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.480
not happen. So what does each set report?

6
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:33.370
Vagal sensory cell bodies sit in two ganglia at the base of the skull.

7
00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:37.710
To pick out one set, researchers use genetic access.

8
00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:44.410
In mice, a Cre driver puts a light-gated channel into neurons that carry one label.

9
00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:47.750
Light then drives only those axons.

10
00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:53.450
Two labels were P2ry1 and Npy2r.

11
00:00:54.283 --> 00:00:59.043
The mice were under deep isoflurane, with the vagus exposed.

12
00:01:00.223 --> 00:01:04.103
Light on P2ry1 neurons suppressed breathing.

13
00:01:04.903 --> 00:01:09.983
Light on Npy2r neurons produced rapid shallow breathing.

14
00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:19.563
Nerve recordings showed P2ry1 axons to be largely fast A fibres, and Npy2r axons

15
00:01:19.563 --> 00:01:21.543
largely slow C fibres.

16
00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:30.187
Activating P2ry1 neurons recruited an airway defence: apnoea, closed vocal folds,

17
00:01:30.727 --> 00:01:33.327
swallowing and expiratory reflexes.

18
00:01:34.107 --> 00:01:36.447
Inflation is a second way to stop breathing.

19
00:01:37.187 --> 00:01:41.747
In the Hering-Breuer reflex, a filling lung interrupts further inspiration.

20
00:01:42.727 --> 00:01:48.247
In mouse ganglion imaging, most stretch-responsive neurons were PIEZO2-positive

21
00:01:48.247 --> 00:01:50.547
and P2RY1-negative.

22
00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:56.090
Light is a test of sufficiency in anaesthetized mice.

23
00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:02.050
It shows what cells can do when driven, not what drives them in life.

24
00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:08.050
A receptor gene used as a label is not thereby the molecule that senses.

25
00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:14.590
And one type, NP19, was only a candidate for the defence reflexes.

26
00:02:15.383 --> 00:02:18.563
So the vagus is not one cable.

27
00:02:19.183 --> 00:02:24.503
It holds sensory axons of many types, and some of them have been tied to different

28
00:02:24.503 --> 00:02:30.103
jobs. Atlases give different counts of types, because their scope differs.

29
00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:33.763
Keep the rule. A label is a handle.

30
00:02:34.443 --> 00:02:40.823
A type is a hypothesis about function, until genetic access, physiology or behaviour

31
00:02:40.823 --> 00:02:41.883
ties it to one.
